  intro={`
    <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">Florence is BamaClean's home. Our office is at 205 S Seminary St, and we've been operating out of this city since 1993 — through the Tennessee River floods that impacted the riverfront district, through the storms that roll in across the Shoals from the west, through the economic cycles that have brought new industries and new residents to the Quad Cities region. We know Florence the way a company only can when it has been part of the community for three decades.</p>
    <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">Florence is a city of genuine character: the birthplace of W.C. Handy and Muscle Shoals Sound Studios' spiritual home, a city with a historic downtown, a growing University of North Alabama campus, and the full residential range from 1920s craftsman bungalows in the Pope Avenue corridor to new construction in the subdivisions off Cox Creek Parkway. Each part of the city presents different cleaning and restoration challenges, and we've navigated all of them enough times to know what to expect before we arrive.</p>
    <p>For Florence residents, our fastest response times apply: 15–25 minutes from call to arrival for most addresses. In a water damage emergency, that difference is measured in gallons of additional absorption and hundreds of dollars of additional remediation scope. Being headquartered here isn't just a point of pride — it's a practical advantage for every Florence homeowner who needs us fast.</p>
  `}
