    heading: "Florence Neighborhood by Neighborhood — What We Know",
    body: `
      <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">The <strong>Pope Avenue corridor and downtown Florence</strong> historic district contains some of the most interesting residential cleaning challenges in the Shoals. Craftsman bungalows from the 1920s and 1930s, many with original hardwood floors that have been through 80–90 years of North Alabama humidity cycles, require the finish-specific, low-moisture approach we've developed through decades of experience with these homes. Original pine floors that predate the widespread use of polyurethane finishes are particularly sensitive — the wrong chemistry or too much moisture causes permanent damage. We do this right.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">The <strong>Westside Florence neighborhoods</strong> include a mix of working-class established homes and newer construction, with carpet in the majority of residences. This is some of our highest-volume residential carpet cleaning territory — families with children and pets, homes where the carpet is 10–15 years old and has been through the full range of North Alabama soil and allergen loading. Hot-water extraction in these homes consistently delivers dramatic visual results and measurable allergen reduction.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">The <strong>Country Club area and Harrington Hills</strong> represent Florence's established professional residential neighborhoods — larger homes, higher-end finishes, and homeowners who expect service quality to match their investment in their properties. We provide tile and grout work in the kitchens and bathrooms of these homes regularly, hardwood floor cleaning in the formal areas, and carpet deep-cleaning in the bedrooms and bonus rooms. These clients tend to be long-term BamaClean customers who've been using us since we started.</p>
      <p>The <strong>UNA campus-adjacent neighborhoods</strong> have high rental density — student housing, graduate student apartments, and faculty rental properties cycle between occupants and need professional cleaning and sanitation between tenants. Property managers in this area use BamaClean for between-tenant carpet cleaning and sanitation on regular schedules.</p>
    `,
  }}
