  competitorSection={{
    heading: "Why Florence Homeowners Choose Their Local Company Over National Alternatives",
    body: `
      <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">Florence's market is dominated by the same national franchise names that operate throughout North Alabama — Stanley Steemer and SERVPRO franchises cover the Shoals from both the Huntsville and Tuscumbia directions. The pitch is familiar: national brand, standardized process, recognized name. The reality, as Florence homeowners who've used both have told us: the national brand gets you a crew that may never have been to Florence before, pricing that escalates from the phone quote to the invoice, and a call center in another state when you need to follow up.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">BamaClean is headquartered in Florence. When you call, someone answers who knows what Cox Creek Parkway looks like in a rainstorm, who knows which subdivisions have the most mold risk, and who can give you a realistic response time rather than a marketing promise. That local knowledge is not something a franchise model can replicate — regardless of what the national TV commercials say.</p>
      <p>For emergency restoration in particular, being headquartered in Florence is a meaningful operational advantage. When a pipe bursts in your home on a Sunday morning, the difference between a 15-minute response and a 60-minute response is measured in gallons of water absorbed into your subfloor and walls. We are the local option — not a franchise dispatching from a hub in another city.</p>
